==Trivia==
*New World Ehen's name is derived from the Japanese word ''ariehen'' (ありえへん), meaning "unbelievable".
**It may also be a reference to ''[[wikipedia:ja:ありえへん∞世界|Ariehen∞Sekai]]'' (ありえへん∞世界, "Unbelievable∞World"), a variety program aired on [[wikipedia:TV Tokyo|TV Tokyo]].
*All Japanese stage names in this sub-chapter are puns using [[wikipedia:Kansai dialect|Kansai dialect]]. In the English version, the only puns are [[Banishin' Tigers]] ([[wikipedia:Hanshin Tigers|Hanshin Tigers]]) and [[Hole Lotta Somethin']] ("A whole lot of something").
**In addition, the stage locations on the map (a jumbled up and horizontally inverted map of Japan) are each placed in a prefecture of the [[wikipedia:Kansai region|Kansai region]] with the addition of [[wikipedia:Awaji Island|Awaji Island]], which is a part of [[wikipedia:Hyōgo Prefecture|Hyōgo Prefecture]].
***Because of this, the "New World" part of New World Ehen likely refers to [[wikipedia:Shinsekai|Shinsekai]] (新世界, lit. "New World"), an old neighborhood of the designated city [[wikipedia:Osaka|Osaka]], which is in the Kansai region.
*In the Korean version, New World Ehen's stages are themed around [[wikipedia:Gyeongsang dialect|Gyeongsang dialect]] and the sub-chapter is named GAGA GAGA, the only Korean sub-chapter name to be written entirely in English.
*The sub-chapter info screen shown when pressing the speech bubble next to New World Ehen in the [[Legend Stages]] menu displays its name as "New World Area: Ehen", which is most likely a mistranslation.

